# PUBLIC REGISTRY, PINNED, and the pin is the point: this machine's global npm config
# routes through the Cadstrom Azure DevOps feed (work), which mints lockfile `resolved`
# URLs no CI or Vercel builder can authenticate against — the 2026-08-24 production deploy
# failed with 401s for exactly this reason, and yarn.lock was rewritten to public URLs the
# same day. Without this file, the next `yarn add` on this machine re-resolves through the
# work feed and quietly reintroduces the problem. Every package this hobby repo uses is
# public; nothing is lost.
registry "https://registry.yarnpkg.com"
